Z||000015||Archie||08-09-2000||12:37 AM||||243 at the wheels.<P>I don't want to throw a wet towel on things here but let me just make a simple statement.<P>First off, Congrats on getting your hands on a real nice example of a V-8 Fiero. I know that you have driven 5.0 Mustangs etc. but I'd like to caution you just a little. The thing that concerns me is that the first thing you are doing with the car when you get it is to take it to a Dyno pull. No offence or anything but that action could be an indication that you plan on raising hell with that car right from the start. I am very interested to hear about your results etc. but I'd like to caution you to get used to the car before raising too much hell on the street. You're gonna find that if you jump in this thing, & give her hell, like you would your 6 banger Fiero you may find yourself in over your head real quick.<P>I resently had a customer who had me install a very nice, very fast engine into his pristine, one owner, 87 GT. Less than 140 miles later he had totalled it after a drag race with a LS1 Camaro. He won the race & best of all he lived.<P>My wish is that you allow yourself to "Learn" the car, drive it normal, then work your way up to driving it real hard. No one is going to take it away from you. You don't have to beat everybody in town in the first week.<P>We all want you to really enjoy the car, we also want you to be safe.<P>Archie<P>||||reg||1
Z||000016||HYPTNOTiSE||08-09-2000||01:14 AM||||Good post Archie, i agree 100%!  My buddy just got his 4.6 DOHC mustang back. He said he has receipts for 50,000 he invested(poured) into the car. It's votech supercharged with an S trim pushing 18psi boost, and all kinds of engine work, a saleen body kit and 18 inch wheels, and sorts of nasty stuff. he's receipts are in a 3 ring binder.  Within the first week of getting it back, he romped on it really good, and when he hit third gear the car shimmyed hard, and he lost it.  He wasn't used to his car yet. he ran it off the road into a ditch and tore up a control arm, knuckle, wheel, and his new saleen body kit.  Very costly mistake.<P>Not saying that i think it's a bad idea to get it dyno tested(i wanna see what it does), but just be careful man. <P><P>------------------<BR>       Mike LeCompte<BR>86 Fiero GT 3.2L w/ Nitrous<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.tcac.net/~daddyg/hypsig.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000017||BBBAD GT||08-09-2000||07:34 AM||||Thanks for the concern guys, and trust me, you don't have anything to be worried about.<P>The dyno session would of never happend, but Travis is the guy who set it all up, and since it'll only be 20 minutes from where I'll be at, I couldn't refuse it.  <P>I guess if you really knew me, 'raising hell' would be the last thing I do.  I've never street raced, even tho I've been taunted several several times.  The dragstrip is where it all should be taken, period.  The motor isn't the only reason I'm buying this Fiero.<P>The irony in this (and makes me laugh inside) is that I'm probably one of the most conservative guys on here (being a 32 yr old CFO of a $650+ million regional bank) and everyone thinks the first thing I'm going to do is street race with the high schoolers.  <P>Like I said, you have nothing to be worried about, but thanks for the concern again   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P><P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/BBBAD_GT_SIG.gif">  <P><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/Fiero.htm" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD GT</A><BR><A HREF="http://scribers.midwest.net/bbbad50/" TARGET=_blank>BBBAD 5.0</A>||||reg||1
